Environ Microbiol</source><volume>68</volume><fpage>4623</fpage><lpage>4628</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12200321</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="pntd.0000002-Marsollier3"><label>13</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Marsollier</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Severin</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Aubry</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Meritt</surname><given-names>RW</given-names></name><name><surname>Saint Andre</surname><given-names>JP</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2004</year><article-title>Aquatic snails, passive hosts of Mycobacterium ulcerans.</article-title><source>Appl Environ Microbiol</source><volume>70</volume><fpage>6296</fpage><lpage>6298</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15466578</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="pntd.0000002-Marsollier4"><label>14</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Marsollier</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Aubry</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Coutanceau</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Andre</surname><given-names>JP</given-names></name><name><surname>Small</surname><given-names>PL</given-names></name><name><surname>Milon</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>Colonization of the salivary glands of Naucoris cimicoides by Mycobacterium ulcerans requires host plasmatocytes and a macrolide toxin, mycolactone.</article-title><source>Cell Microbiol</source><volume>7</volume><fpage>935</fpage><lpage>943</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15953026</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="pntd.0000002-Carey1"><label>15</label><element-citation publication-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Carey</surname><given